  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q31-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "31",
    "prompt": "A florist has an endless supply of tulips, roses, daisies and lilies. Mary wants to make a bouquet of flowers, and wants at least one of each type of flower.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q31-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that the number of possible bouquets of $n$ flowers is the coefficient of $x^n$ in the expansion of $$(x+x^2+x^3+\\cdots)^4.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Each flower type contributes the series $x+x^2+x^3+\\cdots$. Multiplying the four series counts bouquets by total number of flowers, so the coefficient of $x^n$ counts bouquets of $n$ flowers.",
          "worked": "For each flower type, choosing $r\\geq1$ flowers is represented by $x^r$, giving the series $x+x^2+x^3+\\cdots$.\n\nThere are four flower types, so all selections are represented by $(x+x^2+x^3+\\cdots)^4$. A product term $x^a x^b x^c x^d=x^{a+b+c+d}$ represents a bouquet with positive numbers $a,b,c,d$ of the four types. Each quantity selection contributes once. Thus the coefficient of $x^n$ counts exactly the bouquets with $n$ flowers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q31-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the number of possible bouquets of 8 flowers Mary can make.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$35$ possible bouquets.\n\nRead the $x^8$ coefficient after multiplying the supplied reciprocal-power expansion by $x^4$.",
          "worked": "Using question 30,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+x^2+x^3+\\cdots)^4&=x^4(1+4x+10x^2+20x^3+35x^4+\\cdots)\\\\(x+x^2+x^3+\\cdots)^4&=x^4+4x^5+10x^6+20x^7+35x^8+\\cdots.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x^8$ is $35$, so Mary can make $35$ possible bouquets.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
